<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕ-armo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, l, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Aliquem, <i>to
			disarm</i> (except in particip., late Lat. for armis spoliare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dearmatus exercitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
				4</span></i>
			. 10, 7.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Aliquid, <i>to deprive of power, blunt</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pharetram expilet, sagittas dearmet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 172, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
